id: pm-rl-avwn
title: "Coverage gate diverges on the runner: readFileSync(0) on stdin throws EAGAIN locally but returns empty on the CI pipe"
description: "The coverage gate passes locally (100%) but can report 99.97% line / 99.94% branch on the CI runner. The root cause is index.ts logRun reading stdin via readFileSync(path ?? 0, 'utf8'). Under node --test the local child process has fd 0 as a non-blocking socket, so readFileSync(0) throws EAGAIN. On the CI runner fd 0 is a pipe at EOF, so readFileSync(0) returns empty string. The stdin test therefore takes the catch branch locally and the try-succeed branch on CI, making the gate measure different code in each place."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-27T21:00:29.144Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-27T21:39:28.065Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-27T21:07:44.659Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-27T21:07:44.659Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T21:07:33.773Z",pi-agent,"Measured: locally readFileSync(0) on fd 0 (a socket under node --test) throws EAGAIN; on a CI pipe at EOF it returns empty string. The logRun stdin test therefore took the catch branch locally and the try-succeed branch on CI. Fixed by extracting readStdin() with an injectable read parameter: EAGAIN is treated as empty input so both environments take the same path. Three new tests cover the success, EAGAIN, and non-EAGAIN error branches deterministically. npm run coverage exits 0 with 17 files at 100/100/100."
  "2026-08-27T21:39:28.065Z","harness:pi","Follow-up: replaced the EAGAIN normalisation with a real async read-to-EOF. The EAGAIN->empty-string mapping was a data-loss bug (CodeRabbit unbraind/pm-rl#17): a slow producer pausing before writing surfaced as EAGAIN under a non-blocking stdin, so its valid NDJSON was discarded as an empty stream. readStdin is now async (stream: AsyncIterable<string|Uint8Array> = process.stdin) => Promise<string>, draining the iterable until it ends. logRun awaits readStdin(stdinSource.stream), a module-level injectable source so tests never block on the runner's fd 0. The integration test that read real stdin now injects an empty-ended iterable. New unit tests cover string chunks, Uint8Array chunks, empty stream, multi-chunk concatenation, and a slow producer waited past a setTimeout tick. Coverage 100/100/100. No EAGAIN special case remains."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,"Extracted readStdin() to handle EAGAIN from readFileSync(0) on a socket,making stdin reads deterministic across environments"
  test/index.test.ts,project,"Added three readStdin tests covering success,EAGAIN,and non-EAGAIN error branches with injected read functions"
close_reason: fixed
